{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff","id":1549160,"title":"Would have been cool if there was a tradition that focused on animating stuff.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-11T11:46:33-07:00","id":1549160,"title":"Would have been cool if there was a tradition that focused on animating stuff.","content":"Everyone knows what Elemental Mastery is, but imagine if there was an entire blood magic tradition based on it. A talking table that can walk, a piano that runs around and bites people like a dog. Like in those old cartoons where the inanimate objects and forces would suddenly act like people or animals. Imagine just walking into a Tremere chantry and everything is alive, moving, and talking. The couldron tells the Tremere alchemist that they're using the wrong ingredients. Or the Chandelier judges you for how you look. Or the blood packs cut you off because you've been drinking too much. The air itself always has something to complain about.<br /> <br /> I also think that it would have be a pretty good parallel for spirits and wraiths. Also, I don't know if this was mentioned before, but Elemental mastery and the Green path are somehow really good and interesting at all levels. Usually the majority of the paths, at least in my opinion aren't that great. But for some reason these two are pretty nice.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://filedata/fetch?filedataid=1810\" target=\"_blank\"><a href=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1810\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1810_1741715085635_771\" width=\"116\" height=\"88\" data-align=\"none\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1810&amp;type=thumb\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=