l\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1817\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1817&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-11-2025, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T13:32:08-07:00","id":1549161,"title":"","content":"The notion is amusing, but for my money it doesn\u2019t really say \u2018Blood Magic\u2019 so much as it does \u2018Hocus Pocus\u2019 - for my money this is a form of magic that fails to say \u2018Vampire\u2019, as opposed to \u2018Wizard\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T13:54:09-07:00","id":1549165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549161#post1549161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The notion is amusing, but for my money it doesn\u2019t really say \u2018Blood Magic\u2019 so much as it does \u2018Hocus Pocus\u2019 - for my money this is a form of magic that fails to say \u2018Vampire\u2019, as opposed to \u2018Wizard\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, blood magic in general is &quot;hocus pocus&quot;. I would go as far as to say, all of blood magic is really just &quot;hocus pocus&quot;; path of flames, mercury, alchemy, conjuring, transmuatation, neptunes might, technomancy, spirit manipulation, Abyss Mytcism, Koldun sorcery, etc. Plus, there's disciplines that don't really feel like they would belong to vampires either; like vicissitude, as well as auspex that allows astral projection, and serpentis too.<br /> <br /> If you practice blood magic, you're pretty much a vampire wizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T15:04:04-07:00","id":1549167,"title":"","content":"While I agree with Atticus here, there are ways to make it more thematic. Like the big oil painting that watches you as you move, or floor boards trying to grab you as you walk over them. It becomes very on brand once you apply animation to statues and such. Golems and other constructs have a place in Hermetic tradition for the Tremere, and the Setites even have their own Path for Ushabti.<br /> <br /> I had a Tremere character who was making constructs when he was off the clock for Clan business, pretty much as a hobby. Animated dolls work great to freak out visitors to the Chantry, and statues/golems are a bargain alternative for when your Lord doesn't give you perms for a Gargoyle. Don't underestimate the shock value of having a Weeping Angel guard your library.<br /> <br /> I think pairing Elemental Mastery with Green Path has some merit. Both Paths are good for the witch and warlock type of blood mage, and if you put animated clutter into a witch hut it doesn't feel as out of place as in a stately Chantry full of hermetics who approach magic like science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T15:11:20-07:00","id":1549168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff#post1549160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone knows what Elemental Mastery is, but imagine if there was an entire blood magic tradition based on it. A talking table that can walk, a piano that runs around and bites people like a dog. Like in those old cartoons where the inanimate objects and forces would suddenly act like people or animals. Imagine just walking into a Tremere chantry and everything is alive, moving, and talking. The couldron tells the Tremere alchemist that they're using the wrong ingredients. Or the Chandelier judges you for how you look. Or the blood packs cut you off because you've been drinking too much. The air itself always has something to complain about.<br /> <br /> I also think that it would have be a pretty good parallel for spirits and wraiths. Also, I don't know if this was mentioned before, but Elemental mastery and the Green path are somehow really good and interesting at all levels. Usually the majority of the paths, at least in my opinion aren't that great. But for some reason these two are pretty nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is called Koldunic Sorcery<br /> A level 1 Rite actually, retty simple, called <b>Hospitality</b><br /> The Koldun awakens the spirits in an area attuned to him, like his Haven, animating the objects and granting them limited sentience. The objects speak if spoken to and sometimes even when the Koldun does not command<br /> <br /> But in a sense Akhu, Settie Sorcery do something similar with the Ushabti as Voidshaper pointed out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T17:57:54-07:00","id":1549174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549168#post1549168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is called Koldunic Sorcery<br /> A level 1 Rite actually, retty simple, called <b>Hospitality</b><br /> The Koldun awakens the spirits in an area attuned to him, like his Haven, animating the objects and granting them limited sentience. The objects speak if spoken to and sometimes even when the Koldun does not command<br /> <br /> But in a sense Akhu, Settie Sorcery do something similar with the Ushabti as Voidshaper pointed out</div> </div> </div> </div>Was thinking a bit more toy story or brave little toaster ya know? I guess Ushabti could do that at level 4 and 5, but it's not the exact feel. We have flesh monstrosities because of the tzmisce, so it feels right to counter the absurdaty through the use of animated talking toys and appliances.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-11-2025, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T17:58:40-07:00","id":1549175,"title":"","content":"[Deleted] Sent the same thing twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-12-2025, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T18:01:22-07:00","id":1549176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549167#post1549167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with Atticus here, there are ways to make it more thematic. Like the big oil painting that watches you as you move, or floor boards trying to grab you as you walk over them. It becomes very on brand once you apply animation to statues and such. Golems and other constructs have a place in Hermetic tradition for the Tremere, and the Setites even have their own Path for Ushabti.<br /> <br /> I had a Tremere character who was making constructs when he was off the clock for Clan business, pretty much as a hobby. Animated dolls work great to freak out visitors to the Chantry, and statues/golems are a bargain alternative for when your Lord doesn't give you perms for a Gargoyle. Don't underestimate the shock value of having a Weeping Angel guard your library.<br /> <br /> I think pairing Elemental Mastery with Green Path has some merit. Both Paths are good for the witch and warlock type of blood mage, and if you put animated clutter into a witch hut it doesn't feel as out of place as in a stately Chantry full of hermetics who approach magic like science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was thinking more toy story or brave little toaster, somethin to balance out the absurdaity of stuff like tzmisce flesh monsters with the amsurdity of almost cartoon like entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T11:19:12-07:00","id":1549196,"title":"","content":"....<br /> <br /> You know that stuff like Szlachta and Vozhd are supposed to be *horrifying* right? Not 'absurd.'<br /> <br /> A Storyteller may not always do a good job of selling it, but Tzimisce fleshcrafting is supposed to be the stuff of nightmares. Like 'The Thing.'<br /> <br /> [insert generic &quot;do whatever you want at your table disclaimer&quot;], but the whole point that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a> was trying to make is that VtM is typically going more for a creepy horror vibe that cartoonish and comical. Not many people would *want* to evoke &quot;The Brave Little Toaster&quot; in their VtM experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T13:12:16-07:00","id":1549199,"title":"","content":"One should also admit to being worried about Blood Magic coming across as too MAGE - the Old World of Darkness should definitely have a vein of Dark Comedy to keep things from getting too stale, but I do prefer that the powers associated with each Supernatural type be specific, rather than generic (A vampire should be able to do things a Mage cannot and the latter should be able to do things a Garou could scarcely dream of and so on).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a vampire who tries to animate the inanimate with the horrifying power of Blood Magic and finds the painfully-qualified success of this endeavour HILARIOUS (or just keeps trying in a variety of increasingly horrible ways - for example, by making chairs out of dead bodies* - but repeatedly failing) might be the sort of horror comedy material that really fits my mental image of \u2018Vampire Sorcery\u2019 and the World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> <br /> *Thaddeus the Indefatigable would <i>never</i> kill people just to turn them into furniture of course - why would he need to, people keep leaving dead bodies all over the place, he\u2019s just \u2018upcycling\u2019 them.<br /> <br /> Sometimes he doesn\u2019t even have to rob any graves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T16:27:58-07:00","id":1549216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549196#post1549196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....<br /> <br /> You know that stuff like Szlachta and Vozhd are supposed to be *horrifying* right? Not 'absurd.'<br /> <br /> A Storyteller may not always do a good job of selling it, but Tzimisce fleshcrafting is supposed to be the stuff of nightmares. Like 'The Thing.'<br /> <br /> [insert generic &quot;do whatever you want at your table disclaimer&quot;], but the whole point that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a> was trying to make is that VtM is typically going more for a creepy horror vibe that cartoonish and comical. Not many people would *want* to evoke &quot;The Brave Little Toaster&quot; in their VtM experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that when you have vampires who can do everything from turn into animals to shoot fire, the stuff Tzmisce can do end up being not as horrifying. To me, it seems like a lot of VTM tends to be absurd. Such as how we have vampires who can astral project, or not communicating through the Tor browser. Theres also the sabbat raids, a couple dozen or so sabbat trying to find a couple dozen Camrilla in a city o at least a couple hundered thousand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-12-2025, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T16:41:06-07:00","id":1549217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549199#post1549199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One should also admit to being worried about Blood Magic coming across as too MAGE - the Old World of Darkness should definitely have a vein of Dark Comedy to keep things from getting too stale, but I do prefer that the powers associated with each Supernatural type be specific, rather than generic (A vampire should be able to do things a Mage cannot and the latter should be able to do things a Garou could scarcely dream of and so on).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a vampire who tries to animate the inanimate with the horrifying power of Blood Magic and finds the painfully-qualified success of this endeavour HILARIOUS (or just keeps trying in a variety of increasingly horrible ways - for example, by making chairs out of dead bodies* - but repeatedly failing) might be the sort of horror comedy material that really fits my mental image of \u2018Vampire Sorcery\u2019 and the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Thaddeus the Indefatigable would <i>never</i> kill people just to turn them into furniture of course - why would he need to, people keep leaving dead bodies all over the place, he\u2019s just \u2018upcycling\u2019 them.<br /> <br /> Sometimes he doesn\u2019t even have to rob any graves!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think blood magic in general is just sorcerer stuff. You could argue that most of the clans represent the typical vampire we see, but black magic seems to be clearly way out there. On the dark comedy aspect, it could be funny, but using dead bodies seems pretty unnecessary considering to process them would be worth more time and effort than neccessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T17:42:01-07:00","id":1549220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549216#post1549216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that when you have vampires who can do everything from turn into animals to shoot fire, the stuff Tzmisce can do end up being not as horrifying. To me, it seems like a lot of VTM tends to be absurd. Such as how we have vampires who can astral project, or not communicating through the Tor browser.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see how those things diminish the horror of Tzimisce fleshcrafting?<br /> <br /> I'm not denying that most WoD stuff, VtM included, veers into urban fantasy, less horror. Part of that comes with playing as the monster instead of a helpless victim. But also, fire absolutely has the potential to be horrifying; there's a Stephen King novel premised around how fearsome pyrokinesis can be, isn't there? And turning into animals has been a staple of the genre at least since <u>Dracula</u>, which was a horror novel.<br /> <br /> I'm not necessarily arguing that there can't be some comedy, but it seems weird to me to specifically mention one of the more explicitly gory and horrifying elements and saying 'we really need something based on a children's cartoon to balance this out.'<br /> <br /> But again, to each their own. Probably should have just stayed out of it, but the &quot;Brave Little Toaster&quot; thing really threw my brain into a lurch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549216#post1549216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres also the sabbat raids, a couple dozen or so sabbat trying to find a couple dozen Camrilla in a city o at least a couple hundered thousand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of just don't get the point of this statement?<br /> <br /> If you're saying that aspect is absurd, I'm not really sure why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  formatting error 03-12-2025, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T18:43:38-07:00","id":1549223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549217#post1549217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think blood magic in general is just sorcerer stuff. You could argue that most of the clans represent the typical vampire we see, but black magic seems to be clearly way out there. On the dark comedy aspect, it could be funny, but using dead bodies seems pretty unnecessary considering to process them would be worth more time and effort than neccessary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, If we base ourselves on Dracula as the origin of typical vampire stuff, it is nearly all about black magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T07:30:58-07:00","id":1549239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549217#post1549217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think blood magic in general is just sorcerer stuff. You could argue that most of the clans represent the typical vampire we see, but black magic seems to be clearly way out there. On the dark comedy aspect, it could be funny, but using dead bodies seems pretty unnecessary considering to process them would be worth more time and effort than neccessary.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given that animating inanimate objects would be a fairly niche interest anyway, it doesn\u2019t seem out of the question for any vampire pursuing that interest to be more focussed on the destination than the journey - after all, it\u2019s not as if they have to worry about things like old age or a day job!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more serious note, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> seems to be pointing out, to my mind Blood Magic should specifically be Vampire Sorcerer stuff - a vampiric attempt to circumvent the limitation of the Curse of Cain that manages to push the boundaries, but never quite overcomes the limits of being a corpse animated by unholy magics.<br /> <br /> This is, I freely admit, absolutely quibbling - and grounded mostly in my desire that the Kindred always be Vampires first, whether they like it or not (So that nothing about them is ever quite innocuous, even an attempt to produce footstools that follow you about like an affectionate spaniel).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T17:25:59-07:00","id":1549278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549220#post1549220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really see how those things diminish the horror of Tzimisce fleshcrafting?<br /> <br /> I'm not denying that most WoD stuff, VtM included, veers into urban fantasy, less horror. Part of that comes with playing as the monster instead of a helpless victim. But also, fire absolutely has the potential to be horrifying; there's a Stephen King novel premised around how fearsome pyrokinesis can be, isn't there? And turning into animals has been a staple of the genre at least since <u>Dracula</u>, which was a horror novel.<br /> <br /> I'm not necessarily arguing that there can't be some comedy, but it seems weird to me to specifically mention one of the more explicitly gory and horrifying elements and saying 'we really need something based on a children's cartoon to balance this out.'<br /> <br /> But again, to each their own. Probably should have just stayed out of it, but the &quot;Brave Little Toaster&quot; thing really threw my brain into a lurch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I kind of just don't get the point of this statement?<br /> <br /> If you're saying that aspect is absurd, I'm not really sure why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, wrote this when I was high. What I was trying to get at was that, the horror elements within vtm feel more absurd than scary to me. Like how the vhozd are supposed to be scary, but if you have vampires who can trun into animals and others doing magic, it doesent really seem out of place enough to be considred horrifying. Maybe it's better to say it's superficial horror that's based on more tyle than substance? I guess it's horrifying in the same way getting robbed at gun point is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-13-2025, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T23:27:34-07:00","id":1549286,"title":"","content":"It must be a &quot;me&quot; thing but somehow I fail to see how the fact a vampire can turn in to a bat or do some - arguably very limited form - of magic lessen the horror factor of a lovecraftian monstorsity the size of a building made out of dozens of men, animals backed by living siege engienes<br /> In the Dark Ages it was probably the most horrifying thing anyone could encounter, rising above the misty dark forests of the Tzimisce' homlaned or its massive form lumbering on the battlefield<br /> I mean &quot;normal&quot; things like for example an elephant made armies to shit bricks and build a fort out of it<br /> In the mdoern age it still have the &quot;Awwfuuuuck&quot; factor and most of the vampire's brain just nopes out<br /> As a player/storyteller - as others pointed out the Thing or any other Body/biological horror movies - I think of course it is down to personal taste and I would gladly face a gun any time than have to look up something out of Doom or <i>worse</i><br /> As I said, it is a &quot;me&quot; thing probably and I simply can't see how all of <i>that</i> made obsolete by a few parlor tricks and the ability to fly away as a bat... <br /> Naturally you have every right to not see the horror in it, I just can't understand the why","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T10:09:42-07:00","id":1549309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549278#post1549278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol, wrote this when I was high.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair nuff!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549278#post1549278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was trying to get at was that, the horror elements within vtm feel more absurd than scary to me. Like how the vhozd are supposed to be scary, but if you have vampires who can trun into animals and others doing magic, it doesent really seem out of place enough to be considred horrifying. Maybe it's better to say it's superficial horror that's based on more tyle than substance? I guess it's horrifying in the same way getting robbed at gun point is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fair to say that VtM is as much (or more) &quot;horror-themed&quot; than &quot;horror&quot; itself. At least, whether or not it qualifies as &quot;horror&quot; is going to depend on how you engage with it.<br /> <br /> A lot of the &quot;personal horror&quot; that it's supposed to invoke only comes if you really embrace (a rare intended pun!) the notion of vampirism being a curse: that (near-)immortality is depressing, that seeing regular people, even the ones you love, as &quot;kine&quot; is monstrous, and you treat the loss of your identity to the feral savagery of the Beast as a matter of &quot;when&quot; rather than &quot;if.&quot; If you ignore or undersell these aspects, make it easier to play as a &quot;friendly neighbourhood vampire&quot; or really get into the idea of playing as a &quot;monster,&quot; then it's much easier to treat the whole thing as a power-fantasy, which isn't especially horrifying when you're the one experiencing it.<br /> <br /> I think the concept of <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VideoGameCrueltyPotential\" target=\"_blank\">Video Game Cruelty Potential</a> from TV Tropes has some relevance to the discussion, in the sense that people playing a game often put some emotional distance between themselves and the downright awful things that they sometimes do to the NPCs populating the fictional world. The World of Darkness feels less like horror if you treat it more like a generic power-fantasy RPG and don't put a lot of thought into what it would be like being on the receiving end of the sorts of things that a vampire can (and often will) do to other people.<br /> <br /> Imagine encountering something like a Szlachta or a Vozhd in a dark alley. Not your VtM PC, *you*. It's funny to imagine a Tzimisce turning a person into a chair while they're still alive when it's just a game, but what if *you* came home one evening and saw that one of your loved ones had been twisted into some horrible obscenity of exposed bone and muscle, clearly still alive despite how desperately they must be wishing for death...<br /> <br /> Along the same lines, imagine being chased through the woods at night by some *thing* that turned itself into a wolf right in front of your very eyes, like something out of a horror movie. Imagine being pursued by this creature, stalking you with a malevolent and human-like intelligence despite its beastly shape.<br /> <br /> Or being at home one night with one of your loved ones, and watching them just *spontaneously combust* in front of you, screaming in agony until the fire finally manages to kill them, and having no idea of how or why such a thing might have possibly happened.<br /> <br /> A lot of horror comes from suspense and helplessness. The fear of the unknown, or of inescapable cruelty and predation. VtM gives you less of this experience by default because you are (often) not the victim, but the monster. While there may be unknowns, you are less likely to be completely ignorant of the nature of what threatens you, even from an IC perspective. And to the extent that you are participating in a game with some expectation of giving you a &quot;fair chance,&quot; you can more likely expect to be able to fight back somehow.<br /> <br /> I think it may be that part of why it feels so absurd to you is because you're viewing it primarily from the abstract perspective of a player who can put these things into his character's toolkit, and not imagining it from the personal perspective of a normal person suddenly having their life ripped apart by these strange and mysterious powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T22:40:38-07:00","id":1549436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549286#post1549286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It must be a &quot;me&quot; thing but somehow I fail to see how the fact a vampire can turn in to a bat or do some - arguably very limited form - of magic lessen the horror factor of a lovecraftian monstorsity the size of a building made out of dozens of men, animals backed by living siege engienes<br /> In the Dark Ages it was probably the most horrifying thing anyone could encounter, rising above the misty dark forests of the Tzimisce' homlaned or its massive form lumbering on the battlefield<br /> I mean &quot;normal&quot; things like for example an elephant made armies to shit bricks and build a fort out of it<br /> In the mdoern age it still have the &quot;Awwfuuuuck&quot; factor and most of the vampire's brain just nopes out<br /> As a player/storyteller - as others pointed out the Thing or any other Body/biological horror movies - I think of course it is down to personal taste and I would gladly face a gun any time than have to look up something out of Doom or <i>worse</i><br /> As I said, it is a &quot;me&quot; thing probably and I simply can't see how all of <i>that</i> made obsolete by a few parlor tricks and the ability to fly away as a bat...<br /> Naturally you have every right to not see the horror in it, I just can't understand the why</div> </div> </div> </div>I would just like to point out, that the transformation into a bat or wolf with Protean should be more &quot;American Werewolf In London&quot; rather than poof smoke now there is an animal. That in itself is pretty body horror/horrifying itself. Then there's living shadows that <i>come undone</i> from surfaces with Obtenabration, for whatever that looks like... Thaumaturgy Path of Blood can make someone literally boil from the inside out with Blood Boil, as their veins explode, and their body is cooked with steam trying to escape anyway it can. Vohzd are pretty rare in the modern era, due to the difficulty in making them, and with Nosferatu being a thing, I can't see Szlachta being all that much more horrifying to other Kindred. Hell Szlachta aren't even guaranteed to be Appearance 0.<br /> <br /> As far as animate objects being horrifying.. check out Puppetmaster, Phantasm, Annabelle, or The Boy.<br /> <br /> As for Path of Animation, take Path of Biothaumaturgy 3-5, and rename it, have it apply to inanimate objects only, with each rank deciding how big an item can be. Rank 1, something like the size of a small coin (Penny) up to Rank 5 being like something like.. a Car (hey looks its Christine..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","user":"Aydoo","date":". 03-19-2025, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T23:46:44-07:00","id":1549437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549436#post1549436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just like to point out, that the transformation into a bat or wolf with Protean should be more &quot;American Werewolf In London&quot; rather than poof smoke now there is an animal. That in itself is pretty body horror/horrifying itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is true, from a certain point of view, but from another... not that much<br /> I mean <b>Shape of the Beast</b> is ... pretty quick. The transformation requires three turns to complete (spending additional blood points reduces the time of transformation by one turn per point spent, to a minimum of one).<br /> and a turn is around... 3 seconds? (never really was set in stone, usually it is said it is around that, but I must admit heard longer turns, depending on the situation)<br /> And <b><b>Quickshift </b>(Protean \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Vicissitude \u2022\u2022) </b> invoke a Protean transformation into the form of a beast in response to the actions of an aggressor and <i>instantly</i> transform into the shape of a beast.<br /> In any case, it is simply too quick to be really that body horror invoking terrifying sight<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it is not scary (and the rest you listed are indeed terrible to behold) juts it is not really lessen the horror-factor of a kaiju sized abomination made from a plethora of beasts and humans shaped in to a living siege engine rampaging on the battlefield<br /> <br /> And, yes, animated things are horrifying, but it was a brave little toaster level of &quot;fun&quot; in this case what sparked the whole conversation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 03-19-2025, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T20:15:43-07:00","id":1549494,"title":"","content":"I recall in the Gehenna book, one of the scenarios introduced a new Antediluvian called &quot;The Shaper&quot; who possessed the ability to animate and reshape inanimate objects. So there was at least some idea for some sort of Discipline that focused on animating things by the end of the original VtM line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-29T12:52:24-07:00","id":1551335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549494#post1549494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall in the Gehenna book, one of the scenarios introduced a new Antediluvian called &quot;The Shaper&quot; who possessed the ability to animate and reshape inanimate objects. So there was at least some idea for some sort of Discipline that focused on animating things by the end of the original VtM line.</div> </div> </div> </div>THats actually pretty cool, I would have loved it if they made a clan for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-29T12:53:14-07:00","id":1551336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549160-would-have-been-cool-if-there-was-a-tradition-that-focused-on-animating-stuff?p=1549309#post1549309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it may be that part of why it feels so absurd to you is because you're viewing it primarily from the abstract perspective of a player who can put these things into his character's toolkit, and not imagining it from the personal perspective of a normal person suddenly having their life ripped apart by these strange and mysterious powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is probably the reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}